NNAAMMEE
     eenniicc — VIC Ethernet NIC driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee iifflliibb
           ddeevviiccee eenniicc

     To load the driver as a module at run-time, run the following command as
     root:

           kldload if_enic

     To load the driver as a module at boot time, place the following lines in
     loader.conf(5):

           if_enic_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The eenniicc driver provides support for Cisco Virtual Interface Card.  Sup‐
     port is limited to basic network connectivity.  Media is controlled by
     the NIC itself since there can be multiple virtual PCI NIC devices ex‐
     posed to the PCI bus.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The eenniicc driver should supports all known Cisco VIC cards.

CCOONNFFIIGGUURRAATTIIOONN
     The eenniicc network interface is configured using ifconfig(8) and the
     sysctl(8) tree at dev.enic.<N>.  All configurable entries are also tun‐
     ables, and can be put directly into the loader.conf(5) for persistent
     configuration.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     ifconfig(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The eenniicc device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 14.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The eenniicc driver was written by Cisco UCS team based of the DPDK driver.

